@startuml protocol_flow
' Acceptance-protocol figure. Render with:
'   java -jar plantuml.jar figures/protocol_flow.puml

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #444444
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #444444
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFCEF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam NoteFontSize 11
skinparam TitleFontSize 14

title Acceptance requires two independent verdicts

start

:**Candidate netlist**
<size:10>from any generator</size>;

fork
  :**Layer 1**
  **provenance & identity audit**
  ====
  <size:10>reads: netlist + trusted part metadata</size>
  <size:10>//not// the generation trace, //not// an LLM</size>
  ----
  <size:10>local .subckt shadowing the part?</size>
  <size:10>behavioural stub (no device content)?</size>
  <size:10>part never instantiated?</size>
  <size:10>pin roles vs. reference interface?</size>;
  note right
    Static: no simulation.
    Re-derivable by any
    reader from released
    files.
  end note

fork again

  :**Layer 2**
  **behavioural verification**
  ====
  <size:10>reads: the simulator</size>
  ----
  <size:10>converges?</size>
  <size:10>every metric within tolerance?</size>
  <size:10>waveform reproduces its input (THD)?</size>;
  note right
    The gate used on
    its own by prior
    simulator-in-the-loop
    systems.
  end note

end fork

if (both verdicts hold?) then (<b>yes</b>)
  :**ACCEPT**; <<#E9F5EC>>
else (<b>no</b>)
  :**REJECT**; <<#FBEBEB>>
endif

:**Layer 4** — evidence record
<size:10>SHA-256 of candidate + reference</size>
<size:10>each measured value against its target</size>
<size:10>audit flags fired, generation provenance</size>;

stop

legend bottom
  Layer 1 and Layer 2 are independent: a candidate that passes
  simulation can still fail provenance, and vice versa. Acceptance
  requires both. Layer 3 (reference-preserving guard) applies only
  to adaptation tasks and is omitted here.
endlegend

@enduml
